        title: "ZDub's little flags for PMT",
        body: `**The slow way (most local marketing):** the agency checks the ad account weekly, sends a monthly PDF, and the owner sees new leads when he opens his email at night.

**The Nathan way:**
- A lead from PMT's ad triggers an instant text to the lead and an alert to Chris's phone within a minute.
- Zach checks PMT's spend, cost per lead and bookings every morning in under five minutes, so a tiring ad gets caught on day 3, not day 30.
- Every Friday, a three-line note to Chris: what moved, why, and what changes Monday.

Same budget, same ads. The difference is who knows first. (Check what PMT's current tools can actually automate before promising any of it.)`
